/**
 * TestPlan – the doc testing tool's script for this page. Renders nothing.
 *
 * One block per page, placed at the end of the content. It is a single linear
 * script: it walks every testable route on the page in order, reverting state
 * between them, so ordering between procedures and mutual interference between
 * documented alternatives are both handled by the script rather than guessed at
 * by the tool.
 *
 * A route the tool can't drive simply has no steps written for it — say so in
 * prose and move on. There is no "skip" marker: absence of steps IS the skip,
 * and absence of the whole block means nobody has written the plan yet. That
 * distinction is what makes plan coverage countable.
 *
 * Steps use a fixed verb set so execution stays deterministic (no LLM in the
 * hot path). Recognised forms:
 *
 *   click `Label`                     a labelled control
 *   click `A` > `B`                   a path through menus or nav
 *   type `value` into `Field`         literal text
 *   input NAME into `Field`           a value from DOCTEST_INPUT_NAME (never
 *                                     write a real credential or address here)
 *   run the SQL from step N           reuse a fenced block on the page
 *   run SQL: SELECT ...               inline SQL
 *   [resolve: hint]                   escape hatch for a control with no label
 *                                     (a dropzone, an icon, a hover-only edit)
 *
 * Sections, any of which may be omitted:
 *
 *   Isolation   fork / standing / project-level, and why
 *   Setup       fixtures to fetch or create before the walk
 *   Inputs      the DOCTEST_INPUT_* names this plan needs
 *   Steps       the ordered script
 *   Assert      what must be true at the end
 *   Cleanup     exactly what to delete or restore
 *
 * Two invariants the tool enforces, so a plan can't paper over stale docs:
 *   - every `backticked` control name here must appear in the visible prose
 *   - every visible NumberedItem must be accounted for by some step
 */
---